==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*leuþ}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*leuþą}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*leh₁w-}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|liod}} ({{cog|de|Lied}}), {{cog|osx|lioð}} ({{cog|nl|lied}}), {{cog|non|ljóð|t=verse, song}}, {{cog|la|laus|t=praise}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|lēoþ}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|n|head=lēoþ}}

# [[poem]]
#* '''late 9th century''', [[w:Alfred the Great|King Alfred's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=8sy8OOmW-ZAC&pg=PA135 translation] of [[w:Boethius|Boethius']] ''{{w|The Consolation of Philosophy}}''
#*: {{quote|ang|Iċ onġiete þæt iċ þē hæbbe āþrotenne mid þȳ langan spelle, for þon þē lyst nū '''lēoða'''.|I see I've bored you with that long argument, since you want '''poems''' now.}}
# [[song]]

